# authelia secrets — provisioned as .env.secret (gitignored, mode 0600) by
# provision-authelia-secrets.sh. Do not fill this file by hand; run the script.
#
#   bw login && export BW_SESSION="$(bw unlock --raw)"
#   ./provision-authelia-secrets.sh
#
# The script reads each key from the password field of a Bitwarden item:
#
#   authelia-session-secret          -> AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET
#   authelia-storage-secret          -> AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   authelia-oidc-hmac-secret        -> AUTHELIA_IDENTITY_PROVIDERS_OIDC_HMAC_SECRET
#   authelia-ldap-admin-password     -> AUTHELIA_AUTHENTICATION_BACKEND_LDAP_PASSWORD
#                                     + LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD (same value, two consumers)
#
# (No JWT secret: Authelia 4.38+ removed the top-level jwt_secret; the only
# remaining JWT secret is for password reset, which is disabled.)
#
# On first run (items missing) it generates the keys and prints them — save
# them to Bitwarden under the names above.
#
# WARNING: AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY encrypts 2FA secrets in the sqlite
# DB at rest; rotating it after factors exist makes them unreadable (users must
# re-enroll). Keep the Bitwarden items as the single source of truth; the
# script never overwrites an existing item.
#
# The script also provisions two more entries into .env.secret:
#
#   authelia-oidc-homepage-secret    -> raw client secret of the `homepage`
#       OIDC client: the argon2 digest goes into .env.secret as
#       AUTHELIA_IDENTITY_PROVIDERS_OIDC_CLIENTS_0_CLIENT_SECRET (Authelia
#       env override — the committed configuration.yml keeps its REPLACE_ME
#       placeholder); the raw value is printed for homepage/.env as
#       HOMEPAGE_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET.
#
#   authelia-login-password          -> AUTHHELIA_LOGIN_PASSWORD: the login
#       password of uid=sseifried (Authelia binds as the user). Generated on
#       first run and printed — save it to Bitwarden. render-ldif.sh {SSHA}-
#       hashes it (with LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD) into the gitignored rendered LDIF.
#
# The OIDC RSA signing key pair is generated on the server (gitignored,
# covered by backup-authelia.sh) — see docs/services.md.

AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET=
AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
AUTHELIA_IDENTITY_PROVIDERS_OIDC_HMAC_SECRET=
AUTHELIA_AUTHENTICATION_BACKEND_LDAP_PASSWORD=
LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
AUTHELIA_IDENTITY_PROVIDERS_OIDC_CLIENTS_0_CLIENT_SECRET=
AUTHHELIA_LOGIN_PASSWORD=
